  "text": "Rules have ceilings. Take sarcasm: oh great, another delay scores positive, because the words can't see the wink. Context, too: unpredictable is bad in brakes and good in a thriller. And a word missing from the lists counts for nothing. Still, a rule-based baseline is worth building first. It's fast, it needs no training data, and it gives you a score to beat. When it falls short, models learn from labeled examples. But they still tokenize, clean and count, just like this unit did. And many of these ideas are much older than they look. IDF dates from nineteen seventy-two, and counting word pairs from nineteen forty-eight.",
